    "content": {
      "question_html": "<p>Magnesium burns in oxygen: 2Mg + O<sub>2</sub> → 2MgO.</p>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Calculate the mass of magnesium oxide produced when 4.8 g of magnesium burns completely. Relative atomic masses: Mg = 24, O = 16.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(5)</span></div>",
      "question_image_url": null,
      "mark_scheme_html": "<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Moles of Mg = <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"frac__n\">4.8</span><span class=\"frac__d\">24</span></span></div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">= 0.20 mol</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Moles of MgO = 0.20 mol (ratio 1 : 1)</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Relative formula mass of MgO = 40</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Mass = 0.20 × 40 = 8.0 g</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>",
      "mark_scheme_image_url": null
    }
